story-watch-kept = for Mom
story-found-title = It finds you, wherever you are.
story-found-text = Home Assistant knows you are out. So the message goes to your phone, not to an empty kitchen.
story-found-phone = Mom’s phone, with Nestor’s message
story-found-date = Wednesday, November 18
story-found-now = now
story-found-message = The school wrote back: Friday’s trip is on. Pack a picnic.
story-bodies-title = Anything that listens can be a satellite.
story-bodies-text = A satellite is one of Nestor’s bodies, in one room. A speaker hears and speaks, a tablet shows, a robot turns its head toward you, a camera shows the front door. Each one says what it can do, and Nestor uses it: it answers you through the one next to you. A satellite takes a few lines of Python, TypeScript or Rust.
