story-bodies-link = Write a satellite
story-reminder-title = At home, it speaks in the right room.
story-reminder-text = In the evening, Mom is still out. The reminder she asked for this morning is for Grandma, and Home Assistant places her in her room: Nestor says it there, through the room’s satellite. Without a presence sensor in each room, it uses the main satellite, then writes if nobody reacts.
story-reminder-room = Grandma’s room
story-reminder-said = “It’s eight o’clock, Grandma: your pills.”
story-reminder-why = Someone in her room, says Home Assistant
story-reminder-to = For Grandma
story-reminder-asked = Reminder Mom asked for this morning
story-why-title = And you always know why.
story-why-text = Every word it says is in the household’s journal, with its reason. You can read it again in the admin, at any time.
story-why-journal = Journal
story-why-asked = Mom wants to know when the school writes back
story-why-watch = Watch created for Mom
story-why-match = A mail matches the watch
